when forwardAuth enabled, should add filter to httproute and generate traefik middleware:
  1: |
    apiVersion: gateway.networking.k8s.io/v1
    kind: HTTPRoute
    metadata:
      annotations:
        traefik.io/controller: traefik-public
      labels:
        app.kubernetes.io/instance: RELEASE-NAME
        app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: Helm
        app.kubernetes.io/name: app-name
        app.kubernetes.io/version: 0.1.0
        traefik.io/controller: traefik-public
      name: RELEASE-NAME-public
    spec:
      hostnames:
        - test.example.com
      parentRefs:
        - group: gateway.networking.k8s.io
          kind: Gateway
          name: traefik-public
          namespace: gateway-test
      rules:
        - backendRefs:
            - group: ""
              kind: Service
              name: RELEASE-NAME
              namespace: NAMESPACE
              port: 80
              weight: 1
          filters:
            - extensionRef:
                group: traefik.io
                kind: Middleware
                name: RELEASE-NAME-public-forwardauth
              type: ExtensionRef
          matches:
            - path:
                type: PathPrefix
                value: /
  2: |
    apiVersion: traefik.io/v1alpha1
    kind: Middleware
    metadata:
      annotations:
        traefik.io/controller: traefik-public
      labels:
        app.kubernetes.io/instance: RELEASE-NAME
        app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: Helm
        app.kubernetes.io/name: app-name
        app.kubernetes.io/version: 0.1.0
        traefik.io/controller: traefik-public
      name: RELEASE-NAME-public-forwardauth
    spec:
      forwardAuth:
        address: http://oauth2proxy.auth.svc.cluster.local/oauth2/auth
        authResponseHeaders:
          - Auth-Proxy-Email
          - Auth-Proxy-Groups
        trustForwardHeader: true
when forwardAuth has no appName, should build the middleware from the full inline spec:
  1: |
    apiVersion: gateway.networking.k8s.io/v1
    kind: HTTPRoute
    metadata:
      annotations:
        traefik.io/controller: traefik-public
      labels:
        app.kubernetes.io/instance: RELEASE-NAME
        app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: Helm
        app.kubernetes.io/name: app-name
        app.kubernetes.io/version: 0.1.0
        traefik.io/controller: traefik-public
      name: RELEASE-NAME-public
    spec:
      hostnames:
        - test.example.com
      parentRefs:
        - group: gateway.networking.k8s.io
          kind: Gateway
          name: traefik-public
          namespace: gateway-test
      rules:
        - backendRefs:
            - group: ""
              kind: Service
              name: RELEASE-NAME
              namespace: NAMESPACE
              port: 80
              weight: 1
          filters:
            - extensionRef:
                group: traefik.io
                kind: Middleware
                name: RELEASE-NAME-public-forwardauth
              type: ExtensionRef
          matches:
            - path:
                type: PathPrefix
                value: /
  2: |
    apiVersion: traefik.io/v1alpha1
    kind: Middleware
    metadata:
      annotations:
        traefik.io/controller: traefik-public
      labels:
        app.kubernetes.io/instance: RELEASE-NAME
        app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: Helm
        app.kubernetes.io/name: app-name
        app.kubernetes.io/version: 0.1.0
        traefik.io/controller: traefik-public
      name: RELEASE-NAME-public-forwardauth
    spec:
      forwardAuth:
        addAuthCookiesToResponse:
          - Session
        address: http://custom.auth.svc.cluster.local/verify
        authRequestHeaders:
          - Accept
          - X-Forwarded-Method
        authResponseHeaders:
          - X-Custom-User
          - X-Custom-Groups
        authResponseHeadersRegex: ^X-Custom-
        authSigninURL: https://auth.example.com/sign_in
        forwardBody: true
        headerField: X-Auth-User
        maxBodySize: 1048576
        maxResponseBodySize: 2097152
        preserveLocationHeader: true
        preserveRequestMethod: true
        tls:
          caSecret: auth-ca
          certSecret: auth-cert
          insecureSkipVerify: true
        trustForwardHeader: true
when forwardAuth passthrough set, should add a rule routing the path to the provider service without the forwardAuth filter:
  1: |
    apiVersion: gateway.networking.k8s.io/v1
    kind: HTTPRoute
    metadata:
      annotations:
        traefik.io/controller: traefik-public
      labels:
        app.kubernetes.io/instance: RELEASE-NAME
        app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: Helm
        app.kubernetes.io/name: app-name
        app.kubernetes.io/version: 0.1.0
        traefik.io/controller: traefik-public
      name: RELEASE-NAME-public
    spec:
      hostnames:
        - test.example.com
      parentRefs:
        - group: gateway.networking.k8s.io
          kind: Gateway
          name: traefik-public
          namespace: gateway-test
      rules:
        - backendRefs:
            - group: ""
              kind: Service
              name: oauth2proxy
              namespace: auth
              port: 80
              weight: 1
          matches:
            - path:
                type: PathPrefix
                value: /oauth2/
        - backendRefs:
            - group: ""
              kind: Service
              name: RELEASE-NAME
              namespace: NAMESPACE
              port: 80
              weight: 1
          filters:
            - extensionRef:
                group: traefik.io
                kind: Middleware
                name: RELEASE-NAME-public-forwardauth
              type: ExtensionRef
          matches:
            - path:
                type: PathPrefix
                value: /
  2: |
    apiVersion: traefik.io/v1alpha1
    kind: Middleware
    metadata:
      annotations:
        traefik.io/controller: traefik-public
      labels:
        app.kubernetes.io/instance: RELEASE-NAME
        app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: Helm
        app.kubernetes.io/name: app-name
        app.kubernetes.io/version: 0.1.0
        traefik.io/controller: traefik-public
      name: RELEASE-NAME-public-forwardauth
    spec:
      forwardAuth:
        address: http://oauth2proxy.auth.svc.cluster.local/oauth2/auth
        authResponseHeaders:
          - Auth-Proxy-Email
          - Auth-Proxy-Groups
        trustForwardHeader: true
